Bind the IPv6 ICE components to "::" instead of "0".

pjsua builds the bound address of an IPv6 ICE STUN or TURN transport from the
string "0" (IN6_ADDR_ANY). pj_sockaddr_init(AF_INET6, "0") is not an IPv6
literal, so pjlib falls back to getaddrinfo, which on macOS returns the
IPv4-mapped ::ffff:0.0.0.0. Binding that to an IPv6 socket with IPV6_V6ONLY set
(as pjlib does) fails with EADDRNOTAVAIL ("Failed creating STUN transport #1
... Can't assign requested address"): an IPv6 call with ICE then has IPv4
candidates only and fails on an IPv6 answer. "::" is the IPv6 any address and
parses with inet_pton on every platform.

MacroSIP: applied by scripts/build-pjsip.sh (ADR 0014).

--- a/pjsip/src/pjsua-lib/pjsua_media.c
+++ b/pjsip/src/pjsua-lib/pjsua_media.c
@@ -1230,7 +1230,7 @@
         }
 
         for (i = 0; i < ice_cfg.stun_tp_cnt; ++i) {
-            pj_str_t IN6_ADDR_ANY = {"0", 1};
+            pj_str_t IN6_ADDR_ANY = {"::", 2};
 
             /* Configure STUN server */
             if (pjsua_media_acc_is_using_stun(call_med->call->acc_id) &&
@@ -1317,7 +1317,7 @@
             ice_cfg.turn_tp[0].port = 3479;
 
         for (i = 0; i < ice_cfg.turn_tp_cnt; i++) {
-            pj_str_t IN6_ADDR_ANY = {"0", 1};
+            pj_str_t IN6_ADDR_ANY = {"::", 2};
 
             /* Configure TURN connection settings and credential */
             ice_cfg.turn_tp[i].server    = ice_cfg.turn_tp[0].server;
